 "merge": {
  "definition": "for preference w = (w_M, w_C, w_T): theta(w) = w_M theta_M + w_C theta_C + w_T theta_T, a separate mix for every preference (every sample in Part B)",
  "actor_and_trunk": "mixed per preference; trainable in Part B (theta_x receives w_x * dL/dtheta(w))",
  "critic": "mixed the same way and kept in the checkpoints; never read by the contrastive loss, so it receives no gradient",
  "preference_columns": "every specialist is copied into a preference-conditioned DANIEL with its three w-input columns (first actor and critic layers) at zero, so the mixed columns start at zero and the update-0 network is the plain weight mix for every w; trainable in Part B; w is fed both as mixing weights and as the preference input"
 },
